{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cism_templates",
  "description": "Expression-template library for the CISM-specific pointwise laws of the stage-2 CISM components (stage 2 of the EqESM project; CISM = cismwrap_3_00_002 / cism_main_3.00.002 as built in CESM cesm3.0-alphabranch). Carries the pieces of the CISM basal traction, flow-factor, cap-coupling and temperature-step physics that have no PISM/EqIce counterpart and are therefore not in the EqIce template libraries: (a) the bed-elevation friction-angle ramp of the PSEUDO_PLASTIC_OLD basal law (glissade_basal_traction.F90:256-277): phi = phimin below bedmin, phi = phimax above bedmax, and a linear ramp phi = phimin + (bed - bedmin)/(bedmax - bedmin) * (phimax - phimin) in between (the glide_types defaults are pseudo_plastic_phimin = 5 deg, pseudo_plastic_phimax = 40 deg, pseudo_plastic_bedmin = -300 m, pseudo_plastic_bedmax = 700 m, glide_types.F90:2380-2383), (b) the pressure-corrected temperature construction of the Paterson-Budd flow law (glissade_therm.F90:2596-2598): tempcor = clamp(temp - pmptemp, -50, 0) degC, where temp is the ice temperature and pmptemp the pressure melting point temperature in the same column (pmptemp = -rhoi*grav*pmlt*thck*stagsigma, glissade_therm.F90:2170), (c) the GLC cap import temperature transformation (drivers/cpl/nuopc/glc_import_export.F90:326-333): tsfc = ifelse(tsfc_raw - tkfrz < -250, 0, tsfc_raw - tkfrz) with the -250 degC sentinel clamp, and (d) the pointwise laws of the temperature step (M4, lane row 5): the pressure melting point temperature (cism_pmp_temp, glissade_therm.F90:2163-2174), the layer internal melt rate of the TEMP_PROGNOSTIC melt cap (cism_internal_melt_rate, F90:2127-2155, with the temperature reset written as min(temp, pmptemp) at the call site), and the grounded basal melt trio of glissade_basal_melting_ground (F90:1930-2012): the flux-balance melt rate with the eps11 rounding guard (cism_basal_melt_rate), the freeze-on predicate (cism_basal_freeze_on, F90:2007) and the post-melt basal temperature cap with the freeze-on reset (cism_basal_melt_cap, F90:1979, 2010-2011). The rest of the CISM basal and rheology physics is the same law as PISM's and is imported by reference from the EqIce libraries (../../eqice/stage2/basal_templates.esm: the Bueler & van Pelt / Tulaczyk effective pressure and the pseudo-plastic drag; ../../eqice/stage2/ice_rheology_templates.esm: the Paterson-Budd softness) with the CISM constants bound at the call sites. All templates here are match-less and invoked by name via apply_expression_template."
 },
 "expression_templates": {
  "cism_phi_ramp": {
   "description": "Friction angle phi(bed) of the HO_BABC_PSEUDO_PLASTIC_OLD basal law (glissade_basal_traction.F90:256-277): phi = phimin where bed <= bedmin, phi = phimax where bed >= bedmax, and the linear ramp phi = phimin + (bed - bedmin)/(bedmax - bedmin) * (phimax - phimin) in between. bed is the bed elevation topg - eus [m] (with the CELL-CENTER topg, not stagtopg - the known quirk of this deprecated law, glissade_basal_traction.F90:261-263 and bugs.md #23, reproduced here); phimin/phimax are in degrees and bedmin/bedmax in m. CISM-specific: EqIce derives phi from data or inversion rather than from a bed-elevation ramp (CISM_LANE.md row 8).",
   "params": [
    "bed",
    "phimin",
    "phimax",
    "bedmin",
    "bedmax"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "<=",
      "args": [
       "bed",
       "bedmin"
      ]
     },
     "phimin",
     {
      "op": "ifelse",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": ">=",
        "args": [
         "bed",
         "bedmax"
        ]
       },
       "phimax",
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         "phimin",
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               "bed",
               "bedmin"
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               "bedmax",
               "bedmin"
              ]
             }
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             "phimax",
             "phimin"
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "cism_tempcor": {
   "description": "Pressure-corrected temperature of the FLWA_PATERSON_BUDD flow law (glissade_therm.F90:2596-2598): tempcor = min(0, temp - pmptemp), then tempcor = max(-50, tempcor) - i.e. clamp(temp - pmptemp, -50, 0) degC, with temp the ice temperature and pmptemp the pressure melting point temperature in the same layer (both degC, pmptemp <= 0). CISM-specific construction: PISM's Paterson-Budd law takes the pressure-adjusted absolute temperature directly; CISM clamps T - T_pmp to [-50, 0] degC before adding the 273.15 K offset (CISM_LANE.md row 4: 'small variant in the T* construction').",
   "params": [
    "temp",
    "pmptemp"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "max",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": -50.0,
      "units": "degC"
     },
     {
      "op": "min",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.0,
        "units": "degC"
       },
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "temp",
         "pmptemp"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "cism_tsfc_import": {
   "description": "Cap import temperature transformation of the GLC NUOPC cap (drivers/cpl/nuopc/glc_import_export.F90:326-333): tsfc = ifelse(tsfc_raw - tkfrz < -250, 0, tsfc_raw - tkfrz), with tsfc_raw the mediator field Sl_tsrf [K] and tkfrz = SHR_CONST_TKFRZ = 273.15 K (glc_constants.F90:22-23, shr_const_mod.F90:37). The -250 threshold is applied to the CONVERTED value in degC (F90:333); the degC/K offset cancels in the comparison, so the condition is algebraically identical in K. The clamp is the 'Jer hack' sentinel (F90:328-332): land points where CLM sees ocean send a raw value of 0 K, which the -tkfrz conversion would drop to -273.15 degC; the clamp resets those to 0 degC. The subtraction is written twice because the template body has no let-binding (the Fortran converts and clamps in place on the same array). The mediator-to-model halo conversion (vector_to_spatial / parallel_convert_nonhaloed_to_haloed) is a grid operation and lives in the stage-3 assembly. CISM-specific: no PISM/EqIce counterpart (CISM_LANE.md row 15).",
   "params": [
    "tsfc_raw",
    "tkfrz"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "<",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "tsfc_raw",
         "tkfrz"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": -250.0,
        "units": "degC"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 0.0,
      "units": "degC"
     },
     {
      "op": "-",
      "args": [
       "tsfc_raw",
       "tkfrz"
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "cism_pmp_temp": {
   "description": "Pressure melting point temperature at a given depth (glissade_pressure_melting_point, glissade_therm.F90:2163-2174): pmptemp = -rhoi*grav*pmlt*depth degC, with depth measured downward from the ice surface in model thickness units (m) and pmlt the Clapeyron slope of the pressure melting point (glide_types pmlt = 9.7456e-8 K/Pa). Called with depth = thck for the basal value bpmp and with depth = thck*sigma_node for the column profile pmptemp (glissade_pressure_melting_point_column, F90:2178-2192). CISM-specific only in the constants; the law itself is the standard Clapeyron pmp.",
   "params": [
    "depth",
    "rhoi",
    "grav",
    "pmlt"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "-",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 0.0,
      "units": "degC"
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "rhoi",
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         "grav",
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "pmlt",
           "depth"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "cism_internal_melt_rate": {
   "description": "Layer internal melt rate of the TEMP_PROGNOSTIC branch of glissade_basal_melting_internal (glissade_therm.F90:2127-2155): where the layer temperature exceeds the local pressure melting point, the excess energy melt_energy = rhoi*shci*(temp - pmptemp)*layer_thck (J/m2, layer_thck = thck*(sigma(up+1)-sigma(up)) the CISM layer thickness, F90:2142-2143) is applied to melting with immediate drainage to the bed: layer_melt_rate = melt_energy/(rhoi*lhci*dt) (m/s, F90:2144), and the layer temperature is reset to pmptemp (F90:2148). The max(0, ...) guard reproduces the Fortran branch exactly (which fires only where temp > pmptemp); the temperature reset is a state update written at the consuming call site as min(temp, pmptemp). The column melt rate is the sum of the layer rates, added into bmlt_ground (F90:1298).",
   "params": [
    "temp",
    "pmptemp",
    "layer_thck",
    "rhoi",
    "shci",
    "lhci",
    "dt"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "/",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "max",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.0,
        "units": "J/m^2"
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         "rhoi",
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "shci",
           {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               "temp",
               "pmptemp"
              ]
             },
             "layer_thck"
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "rhoi",
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         "lhci",
         "dt"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "cism_basal_melt_rate": {
   "description": "Basal melt rate for grounded ice from the basal heat-flux balance (glissade_basal_melting_ground, glissade_therm.F90:1930-1935 and 1955-1967, TEMP_PROGNOSTIC branch): bflx_mlt = bfricflx + bhydroflx + lcondflx_ground - bheatflx (W/m2, > 0 for melting, < 0 for freeze-on; lcondflx_ground positive down), zeroed where |bflx_mlt| < eps11 (the rounding-error guard, F90:1933-1935), and otherwise bmlt_ground = bflx_mlt/(lhci*rhoi) (m/s, F90:1961); the zeroing applies to the RATE (the Fortran zeroes bmlt_ground, not the flux), so the division sits inside the else branch. The freeze-on branch (bmlt < 0 with no basal water, F90:2007-2012) is carried by cism_basal_freeze_on / cism_basal_melt_cap.",
   "params": [
    "bfricflx",
    "bhydroflx",
    "lcondflx_ground",
    "bheatflx",
    "rhoi",
    "lhci",
    "eps11"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "<",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "abs",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           "bfricflx",
           {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
             "bhydroflx",
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               "lcondflx_ground",
               "bheatflx"
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       "eps11"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 0.0,
      "units": "m/s"
     },
     {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         "bfricflx",
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           "bhydroflx",
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             "lcondflx_ground",
             "bheatflx"
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         "lhci",
         "rhoi"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "cism_basal_freeze_on": {
   "description": "The freeze-on predicate of glissade_basal_melting_ground (glissade_therm.F90:2007-2012): 1 when bmlt < 0 (the flux balance demands freeze-on), bwat == 0 (no local water supply to refreeze), and the pre-cap basal temperature btemp_in >= bpmp - eps08 (the bed sits at the melting point; since the F90:1979 cap only lowers the temperature, checking the pre-cap value is equivalent to the Fortran's check on the capped value). When the predicate fires the Fortran drops btemp_ground to min(bpmp - 2*pmp_threshold, bpmp - eps08) (F90:2010-2011) and zeroes bmlt_ground (F90:2012) - both carried by cism_basal_melt_cap and the consuming call site.",
   "params": [
    "bmlt",
    "bwat",
    "btemp_in",
    "bpmp",
    "eps08"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "and",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "and",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "<",
          "args": [
           "bmlt",
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 0.0,
            "units": "m/s"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "==",
          "args": [
           "bwat",
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 0.0,
            "units": "m"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": ">=",
        "args": [
         "btemp_in",
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           "bpmp",
           "eps08"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 1.0,
      "units": "1"
     },
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 0.0,
      "units": "1"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "cism_basal_melt_cap": {
   "description": "Post-melt basal temperature of glissade_basal_melting_ground (glissade_therm.F90:1979, 2007-2012): btemp_ground = min(btemp_in, bpmp) (the pressure-melting-point cap), and when the freeze-on branch fires (cism_basal_freeze_on: bmlt < 0, bwat == 0, btemp_in >= bpmp - eps08) the temperature is dropped to min(bpmp - 2*pmp_threshold, bpmp - eps08) so the bed is diagnosed as frozen during the next step (F90:1990-1991: dropping two pmp_thresholds below bpmp avoids thawed-bed oscillations as bpmp evolves, while not going so far that the ice is mis-diagnosed as cold; the min(., bpmp - eps08) guards the pmp_threshold ~ 0 case). The paired bmlt zeroing (F90:2012) is applied at the consuming call site with cism_basal_freeze_on.",
   "params": [
    "bmlt",
    "bwat",
    "btemp_in",
    "bpmp",
    "pmp_threshold",
    "eps08"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "==",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "cism_basal_freeze_on",
        "bindings": {
         "bmlt": "bmlt",
         "bwat": "bwat",
         "btemp_in": "btemp_in",
         "bpmp": "bpmp",
         "eps08": "eps08"
        }
       },
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 1.0,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "min",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "bpmp",
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 2.0,
            "units": "1"
           },
           "pmp_threshold"
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "bpmp",
         "eps08"
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "min",
      "args": [
       "btemp_in",
       "bpmp"
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  }
 }
}